WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.038 --> 00:00:04.664
Bill stood on the slope of Grand Peak. He smiled.

2
00:00:04.665 --> 00:00:07.498
This was the tallest mountain in Mountain National Park.

3
00:00:07.499 --> 00:00:09.240
He was climbing it!

4
00:00:09.241 --> 00:00:11.423
Bill was with a small group of climbers.

5
00:00:11.424 --> 00:00:13.260
They walked slowly in a line.

6
00:00:13.261 --> 00:00:15.386
Everyone was clipped to a rope.

7
00:00:15.387 --> 00:00:18.034
A mountain guide, Mark, led them.

8
00:00:18.035 --> 00:00:19.830
Mark shouted over the wind.

9
00:00:19.831 --> 00:00:21.993
"We're almost at the top!

10
00:00:21.994 --> 00:00:25.577
If you look up, you can see the summit!"

11
00:00:25.578 --> 00:00:28.874
Bill got excited. "Let's go faster!"

12
00:00:28.875 --> 00:00:30.853
He bumped into the climber in front of him.

13
00:00:30.854 --> 00:00:34.108
"Oof!" She fell down, pulling the rope with her.

14
00:00:34.109 --> 00:00:37.825
"Whoa!" Bill fell forward and into the deep snow.

15
00:00:37.826 --> 00:00:39.497
The rope got yanked.

16
00:00:39.498 --> 00:00:41.688
It pulled the next climber off balance.

17
00:00:41.689 --> 00:00:44.910
He fell sideways and slid.

18
00:00:44.911 --> 00:00:47.002
Suddenly Bill felt the rope pull him.

19
00:00:47.003 --> 00:00:51.404
Now everyone was sliding! "Ahh!"

20
00:00:51.405 --> 00:00:54.987
Mark quickly slammed an ice ax into the snow.

21
00:00:54.988 --> 00:00:58.546
The group stopped sliding.

22
00:00:58.547 --> 00:01:02.145
A moment later they were back on their feet.

23
00:01:02.146 --> 00:01:05.104
"Don't try to go so fast, Bill," Mark said.

24
00:01:05.105 --> 00:01:08.426
"It's dangerous. Plus, you could run out of energy.

25
00:01:08.427 --> 00:01:11.222
I don't want to carry you back down."

26
00:01:11.223 --> 00:01:14.644
Bill grinned sheepishly. "Sorry."

27
00:01:14.645 --> 00:01:16.934
The group continued up the mountain.

28
00:01:16.935 --> 00:01:19.526
The wind blew harder now.

29
00:01:19.527 --> 00:01:22.356
Snow began to fall.

30
00:01:22.357 --> 00:01:26.040
It grew thick, blocking Bill's view of the summit.

31
00:01:26.041 --> 00:01:28.749
Mark stopped and turned to face the group.

32
00:01:28.750 --> 00:01:30.999
He looked worried.

33
00:01:31.000 --> 00:01:33.343
Bill wondered what was wrong.

34
00:01:33.344 --> 00:01:37.361
Mark sighed. "I hate to say this, folks.

35
00:01:37.362 --> 00:01:39.686
But we need to turn back."

36
00:01:39.687 --> 00:01:43.205
Bill gasped. "Why?"

37
00:01:43.206 --> 00:01:44.945
Mark held up his hands.

38
00:01:44.946 --> 00:01:47.267
"It's too risky to climb in this blizzard.

39
00:01:47.268 --> 00:01:49.186
We must go back down.

40
00:01:49.187 --> 00:01:51.931
We'll try to reach the summit tomorrow."

41
00:01:51.932 --> 00:01:55.441
"Good idea," one climber said.

42
00:01:55.442 --> 00:01:59.590
Another climber nodded. "I don't want to get lost or hurt."

43
00:01:59.591 --> 00:02:03.231
Bill unclipped himself from the rope. "No way!

44
00:02:03.232 --> 00:02:06.595
I paid a lot of money to climb this mountain!"

45
00:02:06.596 --> 00:02:08.563
Mark stood in front of him.

46
00:02:08.564 --> 00:02:11.006
"Bill, I'm responsible for you up here.

47
00:02:11.007 --> 00:02:14.190
And I'm telling you, this weather isn't safe."

48
00:02:14.191 --> 00:02:17.906
Bill went around Mark and continued up the mountain.

49
00:02:17.907 --> 00:02:21.755
"Come back!" Mark shouted.

50
00:02:21.756 --> 00:02:24.239
Bill ignored him.

51
00:02:24.240 --> 00:02:26.383
He leaned into the wind and went up.

52
00:02:26.384 --> 00:02:28.984
Snow blew everywhere.

53
00:02:28.985 --> 00:02:31.184
The summit was very close now.

54
00:02:31.185 --> 00:02:34.219
Just a few more steps . . .

55
00:02:34.220 --> 00:02:38.143
Suddenly a strong wind blew away some snow.

56
00:02:38.144 --> 00:02:40.488
It uncovered several rocks.

57
00:02:40.489 --> 00:02:45.188
One rock glowed.

58
00:02:45.189 --> 00:02:47.759
"That's odd," Bill said.

59
00:02:47.760 --> 00:02:49.507
He picked up the rock.

60
00:02:49.508 --> 00:02:51.702
He saw a flash of energy.

61
00:02:51.703 --> 00:02:54.607
The mountain shook.

62
00:02:54.608 --> 00:02:57.186
Down below, the other climbers heard a roar.

63
00:02:57.187 --> 00:02:58.893
They looked up.

64
00:02:58.894 --> 00:03:01.846
Snow and ice tumbled toward them.

65
00:03:01.847 --> 00:03:07.921
Mark gasped. "Avalanche!"

